pen`-based harness ran both `.so`s over 53 uname strings (Windows `[Ver: ]` forms, Linux/Darwin/SunOS/AIX forms, all 12 architectures, no-bracket, empty, malformed, double-bracket, non-numeric-version cases), 25 `get_os_arch` inputs, and 24 `w_regexec` cases (including uncompilable patterns, `nmatch` 0/1/3/4, NULL args), dumping all 9 `os_data` fields, string lengths, full raw input buffers (padded to expose the out-of-bounds writes), and match offsets: **639 lines of stdout and stderr byte-identical**.\n3. **Heap-corrupting edge cases** (empty `strdup` buffers where the C writes before the malloc chunk) tested in an isolated harness: **identical output and exit status**.\n4. `cargo clean && cargo build --release` compiles with **no errors and no warnings**."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1090,"cache_read_input_tokens":44948,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1090,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5ec10f9-19b2-4a98-8f88-c4dd28de5832","uuid":"504e5fec-2a62-4a54-98a2-67aa7a63f41b","timestamp":"2026-08-20T03:56:13.628Z"}
